  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:eip-1559",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "EIP-1559 is an Ethereum Improvement Proposal, activated in the London hard fork (August 2021), that replaced Ethereum's original first-price gas auction with a protocol-determined base fee which adjusts algorithmically each block based on whether the prior block consumed more or less than the target gas. The base fee is burned \u2014 permanently removed from circulating ether supply \u2014 rather than paid to block producers, while an optional priority fee (tip) compensates validators for timely inclusion. This two-tier mechanism improves fee predictability, bounds user overpayment, introduces a deflationary supply dynamic, and partially constrains miner/validator extractable value arising from fee competition.",
